<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Kaarta</h1><p class="st-meta">1753 CE – 1854 CE (approx.) · capital Nioro</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Bambara kingdom north of the upper Senegal, ruled by the Massasi branch of the Kulibali, rival of Segou until its conquest by Umar Tall in 1854.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kaarta was founded by the Massasi, a branch of the Kulibali dynasty that lost a struggle for power at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segou">Segou</a> and moved north-west. Around 1753 their leader Sebamana established a kingdom in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahel">Sahel</a> country north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> river, among <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soninke">Soninke</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulbe</a> communities, eventually with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nioro-du-sahel">Nioro</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kaarta was a warrior state like the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bamana-empire">Bamana Empire</a>, with an army of slave soldiers and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bambara-people">Bambara</a> warriors and a mostly non-Muslim ruling class over Muslim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soninke">Soninke</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulbe</a> subjects. It raided and fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segou">Segou</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-khasso">Khasso</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-bundu">Bundu</a> and the Moors to the north, and controlled routes linking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salt-trade">salt trade</a> with the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a>. Under Desse Koro around 1800 it reached the peak of its power.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1854 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-hadj-umar-tall">Umar Tall</a> conquered Kaarta and killed its king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamadi-kandia">Mamadi Kandia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nioro-du-sahel">Nioro</a> became an important garrison and religious centre of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/toucouleur-empire">Toucouleur Empire</a>, and the region later passed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-sudan">French Sudan</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1753 CE – 1854 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:94.59%;width:2.01%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1753 CE – 1854 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nioro</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sebamana, Desse Koro, Mamadi Kandia</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Bambara traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bambara</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mali">Mali</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kaarta, Massasi kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1804&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kaarta" aria-label="Kingdom of Kaarta on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4621 1488 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Kaarta lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4745 1864h0M4830 1933h0M4830 1933h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4941 1744h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4941 1744h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Mali. <a href="/atlas?year=1804&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kaarta">On the atlas 